===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|cōdex}}, variant spelling of {{m|la|caudex||tree trunk, book, notebook}}; compare {{m|en|caudex}} (in botany).

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|kōʹdĕks}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈkəʊdɛks/|lang=en|n1={{R:OED Online|title=codex|code=50043046}}}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈkoʊ.dɛks/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|co|dex|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|codices|codexes}}

# An [[early]] [[manuscript]] [[book]].
# A book bound in the modern manner, by joining pages, as opposed to a rolled [[scroll]].
# An [[official]] [[list]] of [[medicine]]s and [[medicinal]] [[ingredient]]s.

